An OAuth2 / JWT authentication flow. Style: flowchart.

Steps:
1. User clicks "Login" on the Client App
2. Client redirects to Auth Server with client_id and redirect_uri
3. User enters credentials on Auth Server login page
4. Auth Server validates credentials against User Database
5. If valid: Auth Server issues Authorization Code, redirects back to Client
6. If invalid: show error, return to step 3
7. Client exchanges Authorization Code for Access Token + Refresh Token via Auth Server
8. Client stores tokens and makes API requests with Authorization: Bearer <token>
9. Resource Server validates token with Auth Server, returns protected resource
10. When Access Token expires: Client uses Refresh Token to get a new Access Token
